    "result": "Perfect! The fix has been successfully implemented and tested. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Bug Fix: `frai gate init --ci` Flag Passing\n\n**Problem:** The `--ci` flag was not being passed from the `frai` CLI to the `frai-gate` subcommand, so the GitHub Actions workflow file was not being created.\n\n**Root Cause:** The main program defines a `--ci` option globally. When `frai gate init --ci` was executed, Commander parsed `--ci` at the main program level, but the gate subcommand wasn't receiving it since it was already consumed by the parent command parser.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the `gate` subcommand action handler in `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d16/with/t1-flag-bug/r2/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Use rest parameters (`...allArgs`) to capture all arguments passed to the action handler\n2. Extract the Command object (which has a reference to its parent)\n3. Access the parent command's options via `.parent?.opts?.()`\n4. Forward the `--ci` flag to the spawned `frai-gate` process if it's set\n\n**Testing:** \n- Built the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` in a fresh directory\n- Confirmed both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created correctly\n- Verified the workflow file has the correct GitHub Actions configuration\n\nThe fix is minimal, focused, and directly addresses the flag-forwarding issue without modifying the `frai-gate` package.",
